<title>FINLAND: Finnish May C/A surplus FIM 3.4 billion -Cen Bank.</title>
<headline>Finnish May C/A surplus FIM 3.4 billion -Cen Bank.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish current account surplus was 3.4 billion markka in May after a 1.5 billion markka surplus in April revised from 1.3 billion, the Bank of Finland said on Friday.  </p>
<p>It gave the following preliminary figures (FIM bln):</p>
<p>			   May 97   Apr 97  Jan-May 97   Jan-May 96</p>
<p> Current account	 +3.4	+1.5     +8.0	 +4.8</p>
<p> Trade balance	   +4.7	+4.3    +19.4	+17.0</p>
<p> --Exports		+16.4     +17.9    +79.9	+73.9</p>
<p> --Imports		+11.7     +13.6    +60.6	+56.9</p>
<p> Capital account	 +/-0	+/-0     +/-0	 -0.1</p>
<p> Direct investment     +0.2	-1.3     -1.6	 -5.3</p>
<p> Portfolio investmen   +2.0    +/-0.0     +3.0	 -7.1</p>
<p> Other capital	   -9.4	-1.2    +11.0	 -8.6</p>
<p> Foreign reserves*     +0.6	+2.6    -18.9	 15.0</p>
<p>(* Negative figure marks an increase in reserves).</p>
<p>Finland's net foreign debt was 273.8 billion markka at end-May, down by 0.8 billion on end-April. The state's share of net foreign debt was 192.4 billion markka, down from 192.5 billion a month earlier, the central bank said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
